  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = x^{2}\\). For all values of \\(x\\), \\(f(x - 3) + f(x + 3) = 2x^{2} + c\\), where \\(c\\) is a constant. What is the value of \\(c\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "18"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "\\(f(x - 3) = (x - 3)^{2} = x^{2} - 6x + 9\\) and \\(f(x + 3) = (x + 3)^{2} = x^{2} + 6x + 9\\).",
    "Adding: \\(2x^{2} + 18\\), so \\(c = 18\\). The \\(x\\) terms cancel."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nf = x**2\ns = expand(f.subs(x, x - 3) + f.subs(x, x + 3))\nassert s == 2*x**2 + 18\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0]) == 18",
